Yes — Google and Facebook use phone-based verification with SMS or voice calls. That's solid for fraud prevention because:
hard to fake (requires actual phone ownership)
instant confirmation (no waiting for manual review)
automated (no human labor per verification)
What's involved:
SMS/Voice API — you need a provider like:
Twilio (SMS + voice calls)
AWS SNS (SMS)
Vonage/Nexmo (SMS + voice)
Google Cloud Messaging
Flow:
User submits phone number
System sends SMS or initiates voice call with a 6-8 digit code
User enters code back into the app
Code is validated server-side
If match → verification approved instantly
If no match within 10 minutes → deny or retry
Cost:
Twilio: ~$0.01 per SMS, ~$0.05 per voice call
AWS SNS: ~$0.0075 per SMS
Vonage: ~$0.04 per SMS, ~$0.10 per voice call
Setup:
Create account with provider (Twilio easiest)
Get API key and phone number
Add to Netlify env variables
Build SMS/voice send route
Build code verification route
Add UI for code input
The trade-off:
Pro: instant, automated, hard to fake, cheaper than manual calls
Con: requires integration setup, small per-verification cost, some users may not receive SMS
My recommendation: Use Twilio for SMS verification as the primary path (instant, cheap, automated), then keep the manual phone call option as a fallback for agents who want the personal touch or have issues receiving SMS.
