The Netlify deploy errored, with the following guidance provided:

**Diagnosis**

Next.js fails to compile because `src/app/api/parcel-search/route.ts` contains an arrow function that opens a block with `=> {` but never returns the object you build inside it. As a result, lines around [#L78-L85](https://github.com/idxrealty-wq/getreadytopost.com/blob/master/src/app/api/parcel-search/route.ts#L78-L85) start with `dor_uc:` inside a block scope, which is interpreted as an illegal label and triggers the syntax error “Expected ';', '}' or <eof'”.

**Solution**

Return the object from the arrow function. For example, change the mapper so it immediately returns the object literal:

```ts
const results = matches.map(({ property: p, avm }) => ({
